-## 6. What this runbook has NOT been executed through
+## 6. Nobody has to remember: the nightly drift watch
+
+§3 starts with "a **BEHIND** row is what triggers this section", which for the first year meant *a
+human ran `currency` and noticed*. Between two such runs the fork drifted 28 upstream commits and
+315 ciru commits. So the trigger is now scheduled (lane-152, 2026-08-18):
+
+```bash
+python -m arifi_core.fork_currency            # what the nightly calls; the report §3 starts from
+python -m arifi_core.fork_currency --json     # machine output
+python -m arifi_core.fork_currency --selftest
+```
+
+It rides `arifi_core.surface_cadence` (`FORK_CURRENCY_STEPS`) with the rest of the estate's nightly,
+appends a row to `registers/estate-manifest/cron-runs.jsonl`, and bridges `hq` **only when the
+BEHIND set changes** — new drift is news, standing drift is the queue this section works through.
+Its own cron row is GREEN when work is owed, because `currency` exits 1 by design in exactly that
+case and a nightly alarm that is always on is an alarm nobody reads. A RED `fork-currency` row means
+the watch itself broke.
+
+The tokensave graph for this repository is already covered by the `tokensave-currency` ride in the
+same cadence; it is deliberately not duplicated here.
+
+## 7. What this runbook has NOT been executed through
+
+Stated plainly so nobody reads a written procedure as an exercised one.
+
+**§2 HAS now been run, once** — lane-152, 2026-08-18, b10453 → b10481. Everything §2 says about
+picking the base, about `bump`'s legs, about the worktree that holds the branch and the churn that
+blocks `--continue` is written from that run. Four conflicts, all in §2.2's manual path; §2.1's
+`bump` refused at leg 2 exactly as designed and is still not a shortcut past §4.
+
+**§4.5 and the register flip have NOT been run by a bump.** Staging remains HQ + President work and
+no bump has ever driven it end to end.
 
-Stated plainly so nobody reads a written procedure as an exercised one: **the first upstream bump
-through §2 has not been run.** This runbook was written at integration time from the mechanisms as
-they exist, and §2.1's `bump` path in particular inherits `arifi-sync`'s own `build` and `judge`
-legs, which that tool's README already marks unexercised. The first real bump is the test of this
-document, and whoever runs it should fix this file where it is wrong rather than working around it.
+**§3 has been run per-source, never as a sweep.** Each ingest below the tq3/rocmfpx line is
